module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Flat.ElementaryEtaleBaseChange
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Flat.ElementaryEtaleLocalizationComp

/-!
# Residue fields along a stage of a base change, and the prime an étale descent carries

Let `C → B` be a ring map and let `ρ : E → Λ` be a `C`-algebra map. The induced map
`B ⊗[C] E → B ⊗[C] Λ` need not be residually trivial at a prime of the target. It **is**, however,
as soon as `ρ` itself is residually trivial at the prime of `Λ` that the prime of `B ⊗[C] Λ`
contracts to: the residue field of `B ⊗[C] Λ` at a prime is generated, as a field, by the images
of `B` and of `Λ`, and if the image of `Λ` already lies in the subfield coming from `E` then
nothing has been added. That is `Ideal.ResidueField.map_bijective_tensorProduct_map_id` below.

The consequence this file exists for concerns a **descent of an étale algebra to a stage**. Suppose
`G` is an algebra over the stage ring `B ⊗[C] E`, suppose `(B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗_{B ⊗[C] E} G` — the base
change of `G` to `B ⊗[C] Λ` — carries a prime whose residue field extension over `B ⊗[C] Λ` is
bijective, and suppose `ρ` is residually trivial as above. Then the prime of `G` underneath it is
residually trivial over `B ⊗[C] E`. The point is that **the descent itself carries no prime and no
residue datum**, and yet the datum is recoverable: the residue field of the prime of `G` is caught
between `κ(𝔭_{B ⊗[C] E})` and `κ(𝔭_{(B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗ G})`, and those two agree.

## Main results

* `Ideal.ResidueField.map_bijective_tensorProduct_map_id`: if `ρ : E →ₐ[C] Λ` is residually
  trivial at the prime of `Λ` that a prime `P` of `B ⊗[C] Λ` contracts to, then `B ⊗[C] E →
  B ⊗[C] Λ` is residually trivial at `P`.
* `Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_of_descent`: the prime of `G`
  underneath a residually trivial prime of the base change `(B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗_{B ⊗[C] E} G` is
  residually trivial over `B ⊗[C] E`.
* `Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_of_descent_algEquiv`: the same
  with `B'` given only up to a `B ⊗[C] Λ`-algebra isomorphism to the base change, which is the
  shape the descent step delivers.
* `Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_tensorProduct_map_id`: the prime
  of `B ⊗[C] Λ` over a given prime of `B ⊗[C] E` whose existence the first theorem presupposes,
  produced rather than assumed.
* `Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_baseChange_of_descent`: the same
  prime transported to an arbitrary further base change `F ⊗_{B ⊗[C] E} G`, which is the form the
  consumer wants.
* `Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_tensorProduct_of_descent`: the
  previous two composed at `F = B ⊗[C] D`, which is clause (4) of Tag `0CAW` at the ring level
  with no prime of `B ⊗_C D` assumed.
* `Ideal.ResidueField.map_bijective_of_comp_bijective`: residual triviality of a composite passes
  to its **second** factor. This is how the hypothesis on `ρ : E → Λ` above is met in practice: `E`
  is a stage of a factorization `R → E → Λ` and what is known is residual triviality of `R → Λ`.

## Implementation notes

*The scheme-level statement of the first theorem is already in the library, and is not used.*
`AlgebraicGeometry.pullback_snd_residueFieldMap_isIso`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Scheme/ResidueFieldMapPullback.lean`) says that residual
triviality
of one leg of a fibre product passes to the base change of the other leg, at every point; read at
`Spec ρ : Spec Λ ⟶ Spec E` and `Spec (B ⊗[C] E) ⟶ Spec E`, with
`B ⊗[C] Λ = (B ⊗[C] E) ⊗_E Λ`, that is the same mathematics as
`Ideal.ResidueField.map_bijective_tensorProduct_map_id`. It is not transported here for the reason
recorded in `StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Flat/ElementaryEtaleBaseChange.lean` for the companion
statement: the consumer is a ring-level theorem about a prime of `B ⊗[C] E` named by a `comap`, and
transporting would need the identification of `Spec (B ⊗[C] Λ)` with the fibre product on carriers,
the two residue-field bridges of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Morphisms/UniversalHomeomorphism/Affine/ResidueField.lean`, and a
separate transport of the prime in both directions — longer than the proof below, and with the
same content.

*The first theorem is proved by exhibiting the inverse, not by a generation argument.* "The residue
field of `B ⊗[C] Λ` at `P` is generated by the images of `B` and `Λ`" is a statement about a
subfield of a fraction field of a quotient of a tensor product, and proving the subfield generated
by two images is everything would mean handling fractions. What is formalized instead is the
retraction that makes the argument work: `Λ → κ(𝔫) ≅ κ(𝔫_E) → κ(Q)` and `B → κ(Q)` agree on `C`, so
`Algebra.TensorProduct.lift` assembles them into `ψ : B ⊗[C] Λ → κ(Q)`; composing `ψ` with
`κ(Q) ↪ κ(P)` gives the canonical map `B ⊗[C] Λ → κ(P)` (checked on the two tensor legs), whose
kernel is `P`, and `κ(Q) ↪ κ(P)` is injective, so `ker ψ = P` too. Then
`Ideal.ResidueField.map_bijective_of_lift` finishes. This is the same device as in
`Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_tensorProduct`, of which this
theorem is *not* an instance: there the residually trivial map is the one being base changed,
here it is the one doing the base changing.

*No residue-field map is rewritten under its own lying-over proof.*
`Ideal.ResidueField.map I J f h` depends on `f`, and `h`'s type mentions `f`, so rewriting `f`
inside such a term fails. Every identification below is therefore stated as an equality of two
concrete residue-field maps and proved by `Ideal.ResidueField.ringHom_ext` together with
`Ideal.ResidueField.map_algebraMap`, never by rewriting a hypothesis inside
`Ideal.ResidueField.map`.

*Why the algebra structure on `B ⊗[C] Λ` over `B ⊗[C] E` is taken as an instance plus an equation.*
The descent step that produces this data,
`Stacks.Smoothing.exists_smooth_stage_etale_map_tensorProduct_of_indSmooth`, supplies it as
`(Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρ).toRingHom.toAlgebra`, so the equation
`halg` holds by `rfl` there. Taking the instance abstractly and the equation as a hypothesis keeps
the statement usable with any other presentation of the same ring map, and keeps `Algebra.Etale`
and `Algebra.IsPushout` instances for the base change available to the caller.

*Étaleness is not restated.* When `G` is étale over `B ⊗[C] E`, the base change
`F ⊗_{B ⊗[C] E} G` is étale over `F` by Mathlib's `Algebra.Etale.baseChange`, which is an instance;
nothing here wraps it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CAW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CAW), whose proof descends an
  étale algebra over `B ⊗_{C, σ} R^∧` to a smooth stage `R'` of a presentation of `R^∧` as a
  filtered colimit of smooth `R`-algebras
-/

@[expose] public section

open TensorProduct

universe u v w x y z

/-- **Residual triviality of a composite passes to its second factor.** If `κ(p) → κ(n)` is
bijective for the composite `g ∘ f : R → E → Λ`, then `κ(n_E) → κ(n)` is bijective for `g`.

Both factors are maps of fields, hence injective, and a surjection factored through `κ(n_E)` makes
the second factor surjective. The analogous statement for local rings and local homomorphisms is
`StacksDraft.residueFieldMap_surjective_of_tower`; this is the form for primes of arbitrary rings,
which is what a factorization `R → E → Λ` through a stage presents. -/
theorem Ideal.ResidueField.map_bijective_of_comp_bijective {R : Type u} {E : Type v} {Λ : Type w}
    [CommRing R] [CommRing E] [CommRing Λ] (p : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime] (nE : Ideal E) [nE.IsPrime]
    (n : Ideal Λ) [n.IsPrime] (f : R →+* E) (g : E →+* Λ) (hf : p = nE.comap f)
    (hg : nE = n.comap g) (hfg : p = n.comap (g.comp f))
    (h : Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map p n (g.comp f) hfg)) :
    Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map nE n g hg) := by
  rw [← Ideal.ResidueField.map_comp p nE n f g hf hg hfg] at h
  refine ⟨RingHom.injective _, ?_⟩
  have h2 : Function.Surjective ((Ideal.ResidueField.map nE n g hg) ∘
      (Ideal.ResidueField.map p nE f hf)) := by
    simpa only [RingHom.coe_comp] using h.surjective
  exact h2.of_comp
/-- The prime `nE` of `E` is the contraction of `Q` along `includeRight`, when `Q` and `n` are
contractions of a prime `P` of `B ⊗[C] Λ`. -/
private theorem comap_includeRight_eq_of_comap_map {C : Type u} {B : Type v} {E : Type w}
    {Λ : Type x} [CommRing C] [CommRing B] [CommRing E] [CommRing Λ] [Algebra C B] [Algebra C E]
    [Algebra C Λ] (ρ : E →ₐ[C] Λ) (nE : Ideal E) (n : Ideal Λ) (hn : nE = n.comap ρ.toRingHom)
    (Q : Ideal (B ⊗[C] E)) (P : Ideal (B ⊗[C] Λ))
    (hQ : Q = P.comap (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρ).toRingHom)
    (hPn : n = P.comap (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : Λ →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] Λ).toRingHom) :
    nE = Q.comap (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : E →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] E).toRingHom := by
  rw [hQ, Ideal.comap_comap,
    show (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρ).toRingHom.comp
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : E →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] E).toRingHom =
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : Λ →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] Λ).toRingHom.comp ρ.toRingHom from
      RingHom.ext fun y => by simp,
    ← Ideal.comap_comap, ← hPn, hn]

/-- The retraction `ψ : B ⊗[C] Λ → κ(Q)` built from a residually trivial `ρ`: it restricts to the
canonical map on the stage ring, has kernel `n` on `Λ`, and composes to the canonical map to `κ(P)`
for any prime `P` over `Q` and `n`. -/
private theorem exists_retraction_of_residueField_bijective {C : Type u} {B : Type v} {E : Type w}
    {Λ : Type x} [CommRing C] [CommRing B] [CommRing E] [CommRing Λ] [Algebra C B] [Algebra C E]
    [Algebra C Λ] (ρ : E →ₐ[C] Λ) (nE : Ideal E) [nE.IsPrime] (n : Ideal Λ) [n.IsPrime]
    (hn : nE = n.comap ρ.toRingHom)
    (hres : Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map nE n ρ.toRingHom hn))
    (Q : Ideal (B ⊗[C] E)) [Q.IsPrime]
    (hQE : nE = Q.comap
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : E →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] E).toRingHom) :
    ∃ ψ : (B ⊗[C] Λ) →ₐ[C] Q.ResidueField,
      ψ.toRingHom.comp (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρ).toRingHom =
        algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) Q.ResidueField ∧
      RingHom.ker (ψ.toRingHom.comp
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : Λ →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] Λ).toRingHom) = n ∧
      ∀ (P : Ideal (B ⊗[C] Λ)) [P.IsPrime]
        (hQ : Q = P.comap (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρ).toRingHom),
        n = P.comap (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : Λ →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] Λ).toRingHom →
        (Ideal.ResidueField.map Q P (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρ).toRingHom
          hQ).comp ψ.toRingHom = algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) P.ResidueField := by
  set g : (B ⊗[C] E) →+* (B ⊗[C] Λ) :=
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρ).toRingHom with hgdef
  -- `Λ → κ(n) ≅ κ(n_E) → κ(Q)`, the right leg of the retraction.
  set e : nE.ResidueField ≃+* n.ResidueField := RingEquiv.ofBijective _ hres with hedef
  set mapEQ : nE.ResidueField →+* Q.ResidueField :=
    Ideal.ResidueField.map nE Q
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : E →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] E).toRingHom hQE with hmapEQ
  set θ : Λ →+* Q.ResidueField :=
    (mapEQ.comp (e.symm : n.ResidueField →+* nE.ResidueField)).comp
      (algebraMap Λ n.ResidueField) with hθdef
  have hθapply : ∀ l : Λ, θ l = mapEQ (e.symm (algebraMap Λ n.ResidueField l)) :=
    fun _ => rfl
  have hθρ : ∀ y : E, θ (ρ y) =
      algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) Q.ResidueField
        ((Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : E →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] E) y) := by
    intro y
    have h1 : e (algebraMap E nE.ResidueField y) = algebraMap Λ n.ResidueField (ρ y) :=
      Ideal.ResidueField.map_algebraMap nE n ρ.toRingHom hn y
    rw [hθapply, ← h1, RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply, hmapEQ]
    exact Ideal.ResidueField.map_algebraMap nE Q _ hQE y
  -- The two legs, and the retraction itself.
  set f₁ : B →ₐ[C] Q.ResidueField :=
    { toRingHom := (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) Q.ResidueField).comp
        (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeft : B →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] E).toRingHom
      commutes' := fun c => by
        change algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) Q.ResidueField
          ((Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeft : B →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] E) (algebraMap C B c)) = _
        rw [(Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeft : B →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] E).commutes c]
        exact (IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply C (B ⊗[C] E) Q.ResidueField c).symm } with hf₁
  set f₂ : Λ →ₐ[C] Q.ResidueField :=
    { toRingHom := θ
      commutes' := fun c => by
        change θ (algebraMap C Λ c) = _
        rw [show algebraMap C Λ c = ρ (algebraMap C E c) from (ρ.commutes c).symm, hθρ,
          show (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : E →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] E) (algebraMap C E c) =
            algebraMap C (B ⊗[C] E) c from
            (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : E →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] E).commutes c]
        exact (IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply C (B ⊗[C] E) Q.ResidueField c).symm } with hf₂
  set ψ : (B ⊗[C] Λ) →ₐ[C] Q.ResidueField :=
    Algebra.TensorProduct.lift f₁ f₂ (fun _ _ => Commute.all _ _) with hψdef
  have hf₁apply : ∀ b : B, f₁ b =
      algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) Q.ResidueField (b ⊗ₜ[C] (1 : E)) := fun b => rfl
  -- `ψ` restricts to the canonical map on the stage ring, and to `θ` on `Λ`.
  have hψleft : ψ.toRingHom.comp g = algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) Q.ResidueField := by
    refine RingHom.ext fun z => ?_
    induction z with
    | tmul b y =>
      change ψ (g (b ⊗ₜ[C] y)) = _
      rw [show g (b ⊗ₜ[C] y) = b ⊗ₜ[C] ρ y from rfl, hψdef]
      rw [Algebra.TensorProduct.lift_tmul, hf₁apply b,
        show f₂ (ρ y) = algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) Q.ResidueField
          ((Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : E →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] E) y) from hθρ y,
        ← map_mul]
      congr 1
      rw [Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight_apply, Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul,
        mul_one, one_mul]
    | add z₁ z₂ h₁ h₂ => simp only [map_add] at h₁ h₂ ⊢; rw [h₁, h₂]
  have hψright : ψ.toRingHom.comp
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : Λ →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] Λ).toRingHom = θ := by
    refine RingHom.ext fun l => ?_
    change ψ ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[C] l) = θ l
    rw [hψdef, Algebra.TensorProduct.lift_tmul, hf₁apply, ← Algebra.TensorProduct.one_def,
      _root_.map_one, one_mul]
    rfl
  -- The kernel of `θ` is `n`, both maps it is composed with being injective.
  have hθker : RingHom.ker θ = n := by
    have hinj : Function.Injective
        (mapEQ.comp (e.symm : n.ResidueField →+* nE.ResidueField)) :=
      mapEQ.injective.comp (e.symm : n.ResidueField →+* nE.ResidueField).injective
    rw [hθdef, ← RingHom.comap_ker, (RingHom.injective_iff_ker_eq_bot _).mp hinj,
      ← RingHom.ker_eq_comap_bot, Ideal.ker_algebraMap_residueField]
  refine ⟨ψ, hψleft, by rw [hψright, hθker], ?_⟩
  intro P _ hQ hPn
  have hsq : ∀ y : E, g ((Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : E →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] E) y) =
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : Λ →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] Λ) (ρ y) := fun y => by
    simp [hgdef]
  have hcomm : (Ideal.ResidueField.map Q P g hQ).comp mapEQ =
      (Ideal.ResidueField.map n P
          (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : Λ →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] Λ).toRingHom hPn).comp
        (Ideal.ResidueField.map nE n ρ.toRingHom hn) := by
    refine Ideal.ResidueField.ringHom_ext (RingHom.ext fun y => ?_)
    simp only [RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply, hmapEQ,
      Ideal.ResidueField.map_algebraMap]
    exact congrArg (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) P.ResidueField) (hsq y)
  have hφθ : ∀ l : Λ, Ideal.ResidueField.map Q P g hQ (θ l) =
      algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) P.ResidueField
        ((Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : Λ →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] Λ) l) := by
    intro l
    have h1 : Ideal.ResidueField.map Q P g hQ (mapEQ
        (e.symm (algebraMap Λ n.ResidueField l))) =
        Ideal.ResidueField.map n P
          (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : Λ →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] Λ).toRingHom hPn
          (Ideal.ResidueField.map nE n ρ.toRingHom hn
            (e.symm (algebraMap Λ n.ResidueField l))) :=
      RingHom.congr_fun hcomm _
    rw [hθapply]
    rw [h1, show Ideal.ResidueField.map nE n ρ.toRingHom hn
        (e.symm (algebraMap Λ n.ResidueField l)) = algebraMap Λ n.ResidueField l from
      e.apply_symm_apply _]
    exact Ideal.ResidueField.map_algebraMap n P _ hPn l
  have hφψ : (Ideal.ResidueField.map Q P g hQ).comp ψ.toRingHom =
      algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) P.ResidueField := by
    refine RingHom.ext fun z => ?_
    induction z with
    | tmul b l =>
      change Ideal.ResidueField.map Q P g hQ (ψ (b ⊗ₜ[C] l)) = _
      rw [hψdef, Algebra.TensorProduct.lift_tmul, map_mul, hf₁apply b,
        show f₂ l = θ l from rfl, hφθ l, Ideal.ResidueField.map_algebraMap, ← map_mul]
      congr 1
      rw [show g (b ⊗ₜ[C] (1 : E)) = b ⊗ₜ[C] (1 : Λ) from by simp [hgdef],
        Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight_apply, Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul,
        mul_one, one_mul]
    | add z₁ z₂ h₁ h₂ => simp only [map_add] at h₁ h₂ ⊢; rw [h₁, h₂]
  exact hφψ

/-- **A base change along a residually trivial map is residually trivial.** Let `ρ : E →ₐ[C] Λ` be
a `C`-algebra map, let `P` be a prime of `B ⊗[C] Λ` whose contraction to `Λ` is `n`, let `n_E` be
the contraction of `n` to `E`, and suppose the residue field extension `κ(n_E) → κ(n)` of `ρ` is
bijective. Then the residue field extension of `B ⊗[C] E → B ⊗[C] Λ` at `P` is bijective.

Mathematically: `κ(P)` is generated as a field by the images of `B` and of `Λ`, and the image of
`Λ` lies in the subfield generated by the image of `E`, because `κ(n_E) = κ(n)`. The formal proof
exhibits the retraction `ψ : B ⊗[C] Λ → κ(Q)` instead; see the module docstring. -/
theorem Ideal.ResidueField.map_bijective_tensorProduct_map_id {C : Type u} {B : Type v} {E : Type w}
    {Λ : Type x} [CommRing C] [CommRing B] [CommRing E] [CommRing Λ] [Algebra C B] [Algebra C E]
    [Algebra C Λ] (ρ : E →ₐ[C] Λ)
    (nE : Ideal E) [nE.IsPrime] (n : Ideal Λ) [n.IsPrime] (hn : nE = n.comap ρ.toRingHom)
    (hres : Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map nE n ρ.toRingHom hn))
    (Q : Ideal (B ⊗[C] E)) [Q.IsPrime] (P : Ideal (B ⊗[C] Λ)) [P.IsPrime]
    (hQ : Q = P.comap (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρ).toRingHom)
    (hPn : n = P.comap (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : Λ →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] Λ).toRingHom) :
    Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map Q P
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρ).toRingHom hQ) := by
  obtain ⟨ψ, hψleft, -, hφψ⟩ := exists_retraction_of_residueField_bijective ρ nE n hn hres Q
    (comap_includeRight_eq_of_comap_map ρ nE n hn Q P hQ hPn)
  have hφψ := hφψ P hQ hPn
  -- The kernel of `ψ` is `P`, since `κ(Q) ↪ κ(P)` is injective.
  have hker : RingHom.ker ψ.toRingHom = P := by
    have h2 : RingHom.ker ((Ideal.ResidueField.map Q P _ hQ).comp ψ.toRingHom) =
        RingHom.ker ψ.toRingHom := by
      rw [← RingHom.comap_ker,
        (RingHom.injective_iff_ker_eq_bot (Ideal.ResidueField.map Q P _ hQ)).mp
          (RingHom.injective _),
        ← RingHom.ker_eq_comap_bot]
    rw [← h2, hφψ, Ideal.ker_algebraMap_residueField]
  exact Ideal.ResidueField.map_bijective_of_lift Q P _ hQ ψ.toRingHom hker hψleft

/-- **The prime of `B ⊗[C] Λ` above a prime of `B ⊗[C] E`, produced rather than assumed.** Let
`ρ : E →ₐ[C] Λ` be residually trivial at a prime `n` of `Λ` contracting to `nE`, and let `Q` be a
prime of `B ⊗[C] E` whose contraction to `E` is `nE`. Then `B ⊗[C] Λ` carries a prime `P`
contracting to `Q` on the left and to `n` on the right, with `κ(Q) → κ(P)` bijective.

`Ideal.ResidueField.map_bijective_tensorProduct_map_id` is the residue field clause of this
statement with `P` *given*; the content added here is the existence of `P`. It is needed because
the data of Stacks `0CAW` names the prime of the stage ring `B ⊗_C R'` — through the point
`y_σ` of the base change along `R^∧` — and not the prime of `B ⊗_C D` at which clause (4) of
that tag places the point `w`; read at `Λ := D`, `ρ := R' → D`, `n := 𝔭_D`, what this produces is
that prime, which
`Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_baseChange_of_descent` takes as its
input `qF`.

*Why it is not an instance of
`Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_tensorProduct`.* That theorem
produces a prime of `F ⊗[E] E'` over a prime of `F`, and read at `F := B ⊗[C] E` and `E' := Λ` it
produces a prime of `(B ⊗[C] E) ⊗[E] Λ`, which is `B ⊗[C] Λ` only through
`Algebra.IsPushout.cancelBaseChangeAlg C B E (B ⊗[C] E) Λ`. Transporting the prime and both
residue data along that isomorphism is longer than reading them off the retraction
`ψ : B ⊗[C] Λ → κ(Q)` that
`Ideal.ResidueField.map_bijective_tensorProduct_map_id` builds anyway, and it would leave the
conclusion's `comap` stated through the isomorphism rather than through
`Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρ`, which is the map the consumer holds. The
retraction is therefore rebuilt here and the residue field clause is then *quoted* from that
theorem rather than reproved. -/
theorem Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_tensorProduct_map_id
    {C : Type u} {B : Type v} {E : Type w} {Λ : Type x} [CommRing C] [CommRing B] [CommRing E]
    [CommRing Λ] [Algebra C B] [Algebra C E] [Algebra C Λ] (ρ : E →ₐ[C] Λ)
    (nE : Ideal E) [nE.IsPrime] (n : Ideal Λ) [n.IsPrime] (hn : nE = n.comap ρ.toRingHom)
    (hres : Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map nE n ρ.toRingHom hn))
    (Q : Ideal (B ⊗[C] E)) [Q.IsPrime]
    (hQE : nE = Q.comap
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : E →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] E).toRingHom) :
    ∃ (P : Ideal (B ⊗[C] Λ)) (_ : P.IsPrime)
      (hQ : Q = P.comap (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρ).toRingHom),
      n = P.comap (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : Λ →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] Λ).toRingHom ∧
        Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map Q P
          (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρ).toRingHom hQ) := by
  obtain ⟨ψ, hψleft, hker, -⟩ := exists_retraction_of_residueField_bijective ρ nE n hn hres Q hQE
  have := RingHom.ker_isPrime ψ.toRingHom
  have hQker : Q = (RingHom.ker ψ.toRingHom).comap
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρ).toRingHom := by
    rw [RingHom.comap_ker, hψleft, Ideal.ker_algebraMap_residueField]
  have hnker : n = (RingHom.ker ψ.toRingHom).comap
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : Λ →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] Λ).toRingHom := by
    rw [RingHom.comap_ker, hker]
  exact ⟨RingHom.ker ψ.toRingHom, this, hQker, hnker,
    Ideal.ResidueField.map_bijective_tensorProduct_map_id ρ nE n hn hres Q
      (RingHom.ker ψ.toRingHom) hQker hnker⟩

/-- **An étale descent to a stage carries a residually trivial prime, even though the descent
itself carries no prime.** Let `ρ : E →ₐ[C] Λ` be residually trivial at the prime `n` of `Λ` that
a prime `P` of `B ⊗[C] Λ` contracts to, let `G` be an algebra over the stage ring `B ⊗[C] E`, and
let `P'` be a prime of the base change `(B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗_{B ⊗[C] E} G` which contracts to `P` with
bijective residue field extension. Then the contraction of `P'` to `G` is a prime over
`Q = 𝔭_{B ⊗[C] E}` with bijective residue field extension.

Read at Stacks `0CAW`: `Λ = R^∧`, `E = R'` is the smooth stage, `G = B''` is the descended étale
algebra, `P'` is the prime of `B'` that the previous step produces, and the conclusion is the
residually trivial prime of `B''` over `B ⊗_C R'` which clause (4) of that tag needs and which the
descent step does not supply. The residue field of the prime of `G` is caught between `κ(Q)` and
`κ(P')`, and `κ(Q) = κ(P) = κ(P')`, the first equality being
`Ideal.ResidueField.map_bijective_tensorProduct_map_id`. In particular **no enlargement of the
stage is needed**. -/
theorem Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_of_descent {C : Type u}
    {B : Type v} {E : Type w} {Λ : Type x} {G : Type y} [CommRing C] [CommRing B] [CommRing E]
    [CommRing Λ] [CommRing G] [Algebra C B] [Algebra C E] [Algebra C Λ] (ρ : E →ₐ[C] Λ)
    [Algebra (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] Λ)]
    (halg : algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] Λ) =
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρ).toRingHom)
    [Algebra (B ⊗[C] E) G]
    (nE : Ideal E) [nE.IsPrime] (n : Ideal Λ) [n.IsPrime] (hn : nE = n.comap ρ.toRingHom)
    (hres : Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map nE n ρ.toRingHom hn))
    (Q : Ideal (B ⊗[C] E)) [Q.IsPrime] (P : Ideal (B ⊗[C] Λ)) [P.IsPrime]
    (hQ : Q = P.comap (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] Λ)))
    (hPn : n = P.comap (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : Λ →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] Λ).toRingHom)
    (P' : Ideal ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) [P'.IsPrime]
    (hP' : P = P'.comap (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)))
    (hP'res : Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map P P'
      (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) hP')) :
    ∃ (QG : Ideal G) (_ : QG.IsPrime) (hQG : Q = QG.comap (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) G)),
      Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map Q QG (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) G) hQG) := by
  -- `κ(Q) = κ(P)`, by the preceding theorem.
  have hQP : Function.Bijective
      (Ideal.ResidueField.map Q P (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] Λ)) hQ) := by
    revert hQ
    rw [halg]
    intro hQ
    exact Ideal.ResidueField.map_bijective_tensorProduct_map_id ρ nE n hn hres Q P hQ hPn
  -- the prime of `G`, and the three contractions of `P'` to the stage ring
  set w : G →+* (B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G :=
    (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight :
      G →ₐ[B ⊗[C] E] (B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G).toRingHom with hwdef
  have hwalg : w.comp (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) G) =
      algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G) :=
    RingHom.ext fun x => (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight :
      G →ₐ[B ⊗[C] E] (B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G).commutes x
  have hQT : Q = P'.comap (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) := by
    rw [hQ, hP', Ideal.comap_comap,
      ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] Λ) ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)]
  have hQG : Q = (P'.comap w).comap (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) G) := by
    rw [Ideal.comap_comap, hwalg]; exact hQT
  have : (P'.comap w).IsPrime := Ideal.comap_isPrime _ _
  refine ⟨P'.comap w, inferInstance, hQG, ?_⟩
  -- `κ(Q) = κ(P')`, through `κ(P)`
  have h1 : Ideal.ResidueField.map Q P'
        (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) hQT =
      (Ideal.ResidueField.map P P'
          (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) hP').comp
        (Ideal.ResidueField.map Q P (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] Λ)) hQ) := by
    refine Ideal.ResidueField.ringHom_ext (RingHom.ext fun z => ?_)
    simp only [RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply, Ideal.ResidueField.map_algebraMap]
    exact congrArg (algebraMap _ P'.ResidueField)
      (IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] Λ)
        ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G) z)
  have hQP' : Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map Q P'
      (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) hQT) := by
    rw [h1]
    simpa only [RingHom.coe_comp] using hP'res.comp hQP
  -- and the same factored through `κ(𝔭_G)`, whose second leg is injective
  have h2 : Ideal.ResidueField.map Q P'
        (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) hQT =
      (Ideal.ResidueField.map (P'.comap w) P' w rfl).comp
        (Ideal.ResidueField.map Q (P'.comap w) (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) G) hQG) := by
    refine Ideal.ResidueField.ringHom_ext (RingHom.ext fun z => ?_)
    simp only [RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply, Ideal.ResidueField.map_algebraMap]
    exact congrArg (algebraMap _ P'.ResidueField) (RingHom.congr_fun hwalg z).symm
  rw [h2] at hQP'
  exact Function.Bijective.of_comp_left
    (by simpa only [RingHom.coe_comp] using hQP') (RingHom.injective _)

/-- **The same, with the étale algebra over `B ⊗[C] Λ` given only up to isomorphism.** This is the
shape `Stacks.Smoothing.exists_smooth_stage_etale_map_tensorProduct_of_indSmooth` delivers: it
produces a `B ⊗[C] Λ`-algebra isomorphism `e : B' ≃ₐ (B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗_{B ⊗[C] E} G` rather than `B'`
*being* the base change, and the residually trivial prime of the preceding step of the proof of
Stacks `0CAW` lives on `B'`. The prime of `G` is then the contraction of the prime `e` carries
across.

Residual triviality crosses `e` because a ring isomorphism is surjective on stalks, so its own
residue field extension is bijective and may be cancelled off a composite. -/
theorem Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_of_descent_algEquiv
    {C : Type u} {B : Type v} {E : Type w} {Λ : Type x} {G B' : Type y} [CommRing C] [CommRing B]
    [CommRing E] [CommRing Λ] [CommRing G] [CommRing B'] [Algebra C B] [Algebra C E] [Algebra C Λ]
    (ρ : E →ₐ[C] Λ) [Algebra (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] Λ)]
    (halg : algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] Λ) =
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρ).toRingHom)
    [Algebra (B ⊗[C] E) G] [Algebra (B ⊗[C] Λ) B']
    (nE : Ideal E) [nE.IsPrime] (n : Ideal Λ) [n.IsPrime] (hn : nE = n.comap ρ.toRingHom)
    (hres : Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map nE n ρ.toRingHom hn))
    (Q : Ideal (B ⊗[C] E)) [Q.IsPrime] (P : Ideal (B ⊗[C] Λ)) [P.IsPrime]
    (hQ : Q = P.comap (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] Λ)))
    (hPn : n = P.comap (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : Λ →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] Λ).toRingHom)
    (e : B' ≃ₐ[B ⊗[C] Λ] (B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)
    (p' : Ideal B') [p'.IsPrime] (hp' : P = p'.comap (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) B'))
    (hp'res : Function.Bijective
      (Ideal.ResidueField.map P p' (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) B') hp')) :
    ∃ (QG : Ideal G) (_ : QG.IsPrime) (hQG : Q = QG.comap (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) G)),
      Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map Q QG (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) G) hQG) := by
  set χ : ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G) ≃+* B' := e.symm.toRingEquiv with hχ
  have hχalg : ∀ z : B ⊗[C] Λ,
      (χ : ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G) →+* B')
        (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G) z) =
      algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) B' z := fun z => e.symm.commutes z
  have : (p'.comap (χ : ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G) →+* B')).IsPrime := Ideal.comap_isPrime _ _
  have hP' : P = (p'.comap (χ : ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G) →+* B')).comap
      (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) := by
    rw [Ideal.comap_comap,
      show (χ : ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G) →+* B').comp
          (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) =
        algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) B' from RingHom.ext hχalg]
    exact hp'
  -- residual triviality of `P` crosses `χ`
  have h1 : Ideal.ResidueField.map P p' (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) B') hp' =
      (Ideal.ResidueField.map (p'.comap (χ : ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G) →+* B')) p'
          (χ : ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G) →+* B') rfl).comp
        (Ideal.ResidueField.map P (p'.comap (χ : ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G) →+* B'))
          (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) hP') := by
    refine Ideal.ResidueField.ringHom_ext (RingHom.ext fun z => ?_)
    simp only [RingHom.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply, Ideal.ResidueField.map_algebraMap]
    exact congrArg (algebraMap B' p'.ResidueField) (hχalg z).symm
  rw [h1] at hp'res
  refine Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_of_descent ρ halg nE n hn
    hres Q P hQ hPn (p'.comap (χ : ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G) →+* B')) hP' ?_
  refine (Function.Bijective.of_comp_iff' ?_ _).mp
    (by simpa only [RingHom.coe_comp] using hp'res)
  exact χ.surjectiveOnStalks.residueFieldMap_bijective _ _ rfl
/-- **The residually trivial prime an étale descent carries, transported to a further base
change.** In the situation of
`Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_of_descent`, let `F` be any algebra
over the stage ring `B ⊗[C] E` with a prime `qF` over `Q`. Then `F ⊗_{B ⊗[C] E} G` carries a prime
over `qF` with bijective residue field extension.

Read at Stacks `0CAW` with `F = B ⊗_C D`, this is the residual triviality half of clause (4):
`Spec(B'' ⊗_{R'} D) ⟶ Spec(B ⊗_C D)` is an elementary étale neighbourhood at the point produced
here, the étaleness half being Mathlib's `Algebra.Etale.baseChange` instance for
`F ⊗_{B ⊗[C] E} G` over `F`, which needs nothing from this file. -/
theorem Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_baseChange_of_descent
    {C : Type u} {B : Type v} {E : Type w} {Λ : Type x} {G : Type y} {F : Type z} [CommRing C]
    [CommRing B]
    [CommRing E] [CommRing Λ] [CommRing G] [CommRing F] [Algebra C B] [Algebra C E] [Algebra C Λ]
    (ρ : E →ₐ[C] Λ) [Algebra (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] Λ)]
    (halg : algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] Λ) =
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρ).toRingHom)
    [Algebra (B ⊗[C] E) G] [Algebra (B ⊗[C] E) F]
    (nE : Ideal E) [nE.IsPrime] (n : Ideal Λ) [n.IsPrime] (hn : nE = n.comap ρ.toRingHom)
    (hres : Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map nE n ρ.toRingHom hn))
    (Q : Ideal (B ⊗[C] E)) [Q.IsPrime] (P : Ideal (B ⊗[C] Λ)) [P.IsPrime]
    (hQ : Q = P.comap (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] Λ)))
    (hPn : n = P.comap (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : Λ →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] Λ).toRingHom)
    (P' : Ideal ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) [P'.IsPrime]
    (hP' : P = P'.comap (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)))
    (hP'res : Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map P P'
      (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) hP'))
    (qF : Ideal F) [qF.IsPrime] (hqF : Q = qF.comap (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) F)) :
    ∃ (QF : Ideal (F ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) (_ : QF.IsPrime)
      (hQF : qF = QF.comap (algebraMap F (F ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G))),
      Function.Bijective
        (Ideal.ResidueField.map qF QF (algebraMap F (F ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) hQF) := by
  obtain ⟨QG, _, hQG, hQGres⟩ :=
    Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_of_descent ρ halg nE n hn hres
      Q P hQ hPn P' hP' hP'res
  obtain ⟨QF, hQFprime, hQF, -, hQFres⟩ :=
    Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_tensorProduct Q QG hQG hQGres
      qF hqF
  exact ⟨QF, hQFprime, hQF, hQFres⟩

/-- **Clause (4) of Stacks `0CAW` at the ring level, with no prime assumed.** Keep the data of
`Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_baseChange_of_descent` but take
`F = B ⊗[C] D` for a second `C`-algebra `D` under the stage, with `ρ_D : E →ₐ[C] D` residually
trivial at a prime `vD` of `D` over `nE`. Then `B ⊗[C] D` carries a prime `qF` over `Q` and over
`vD` with `κ(Q) → κ(qF)` bijective, and the base change `(B ⊗[C] D) ⊗_{B ⊗[C] E} G` carries a
prime over `qF` with `κ(qF) → κ(QF)` bijective.

Read at Stacks `0CAW`: `Λ = R^∧`, `E = R'` is the smooth stage, `G = B''` is the descended étale
algebra, `D` is the étale `R`-algebra the final application of Tag `0CAU` produces and `vD` its
prime over `𝔭`. Then `qF` is the point `(y, v)` of `Y ×_{T, τ} V = Spec(B ⊗_C D)` and `QF` is the
point `w` of `W = Spec(B'' ⊗_{R'} D)`, and the last clause is the residual triviality half of
clause (4) — the étaleness half being Mathlib's `Algebra.Etale.baseChange` instance, which needs
nothing from this file.

This is the whole of clause (4) at the ring level: the previous theorem took the prime of
`B ⊗_C D` as its input `qF`, and `0CAW`'s own data names no such prime — what it names is the
prime of the stage ring `B ⊗_C R'` carried by the point `y_σ`. The prime is produced by
`Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_tensorProduct_map_id`, whose
hypothesis that `Q` contracts to `nE` on `E` is derived here from `hQ` and `hPn`.

The residual triviality of `ρ_D` is the hypothesis `hresD`; at `0CAW`'s data it holds because
`κ(𝔭_R) → κ(𝔭_D)` and `κ(𝔭_R) → κ(𝔭_{R'})` are both bijective and `R → R' → D` is `R → D`, which
is `Ideal.ResidueField.map_bijective_of_comp_bijective`. -/
theorem Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_tensorProduct_of_descent
    {C : Type u} {B : Type v} {E : Type w} {Λ : Type x} {D : Type y} {G : Type z} [CommRing C]
    [CommRing B] [CommRing E] [CommRing Λ] [CommRing D] [CommRing G] [Algebra C B] [Algebra C E]
    [Algebra C Λ] [Algebra C D]
    (ρ : E →ₐ[C] Λ) (ρD : E →ₐ[C] D) [Algebra (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] Λ)]
    (halg : algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] Λ) =
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρ).toRingHom)
    [Algebra (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] D)]
    (halgD : algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] D) =
      (Algebra.TensorProduct.map (AlgHom.id B B) ρD).toRingHom)
    [Algebra (B ⊗[C] E) G]
    (nE : Ideal E) [nE.IsPrime] (n : Ideal Λ) [n.IsPrime] (hn : nE = n.comap ρ.toRingHom)
    (hres : Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map nE n ρ.toRingHom hn))
    (vD : Ideal D) [vD.IsPrime] (hvD : nE = vD.comap ρD.toRingHom)
    (hresD : Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map nE vD ρD.toRingHom hvD))
    (Q : Ideal (B ⊗[C] E)) [Q.IsPrime] (P : Ideal (B ⊗[C] Λ)) [P.IsPrime]
    (hQ : Q = P.comap (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] Λ)))
    (hPn : n = P.comap (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : Λ →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] Λ).toRingHom)
    (P' : Ideal ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) [P'.IsPrime]
    (hP' : P = P'.comap (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)))
    (hP'res : Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map P P'
      (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] Λ) ((B ⊗[C] Λ) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) hP')) :
    ∃ (qF : Ideal (B ⊗[C] D)) (_ : qF.IsPrime)
      (hqF : Q = qF.comap (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] D))),
      vD = qF.comap (Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight : D →ₐ[C] B ⊗[C] D).toRingHom ∧
        Function.Bijective
            (Ideal.ResidueField.map Q qF (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] D)) hqF) ∧
          ∃ (QF : Ideal ((B ⊗[C] D) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) (_ : QF.IsPrime)
            (hQF : qF = QF.comap
              (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] D) ((B ⊗[C] D) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G))),
            Function.Bijective (Ideal.ResidueField.map qF QF
              (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] D) ((B ⊗[C] D) ⊗[B ⊗[C] E] G)) hQF) := by
  -- `Q` contracts to `nE` on `E`, by the two contractions of `P`.
  have hQE := comap_includeRight_eq_of_comap_map ρ nE n hn Q P (halg ▸ hQ) hPn
  -- the prime of `B ⊗[C] D`
  obtain ⟨qF, hqFprime, hqF₀, hvD', hresQ₀⟩ :=
    Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_tensorProduct_map_id ρD nE vD
      hvD hresD Q hQE
  have := hqFprime
  have hqF : Q = qF.comap (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] D)) := by rw [halgD]; exact hqF₀
  have hresQ : Function.Bijective
      (Ideal.ResidueField.map Q qF (algebraMap (B ⊗[C] E) (B ⊗[C] D)) hqF) := by
    revert hqF
    rw [halgD]
    intro hqF
    exact hresQ₀
  obtain ⟨QF, hQFprime, hQF, hQFres⟩ :=
    Ideal.exists_isPrime_comap_eq_and_residueField_map_bijective_baseChange_of_descent ρ halg
      nE n hn hres Q P hQ hPn P' hP' hP'res qF hqF
  exact ⟨qF, hqFprime, hqF, hvD', hresQ, QF, hQFprime, hQF, hQFres⟩

end
